    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19729" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gnătho</span></b> , ōnis,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γνάθων</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a parasite in the</i>
			Eunuchus <i>of Terence;</i> hence used to denote <i>a parasite</i> in gen., <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Lael. 25, 93 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Phil.
				2, 6, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 3,
			13</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gnăthōnĭci</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., qs. <i>disciples of Gnatho</i>, <i>Gnathonites</i>, i. e. <i>parasites</i>, <i><span class="en">Ter. Eun.
				2, 2, 33</span></i>.</div>
